From: Plain Browser
Subject: [ui] Default browser from the MSIX package: check and set it by the package app's ID

Category: 60-ui. Code lives in //plainbrowser/win (msix_default_browser.*); this patch only calls it. From the
Microsoft Store the browser runs from an MSIX package: Windows registers its http/https handlers under generated
"AppX..." ProgIDs and keeps the app's own registry writes in the package's private hive. Chromium's check compares
the current default with the installer's ProgID (PlainBrowserHTML...), so chrome://settings always said "not
default", and "Make default" opened Default apps for an application name Windows does not know. In a package,
GetDefaultBrowser() now compares the http and https handlers' App User Model IDs with the package app's
(<PackageFamilyName>!PlainBrowser), and SetAsDefaultBrowserUsingSystemSettings() opens
ms-settings:defaultapps?registeredAUMID=<that ID>, the package app's page in Settings > Apps > Default apps
(watching the UserChoice keys as before). Outside a package (portable build) both fall through to Chromium's code.
---
--- a/chrome/browser/shell_integration_win.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/shell_integration_win.cc
@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@
 // found in the LICENSE file.
 
 #include "chrome/browser/shell_integration_win.h"
+
+// Plain Browser: own includes (patches/series), kept together up here so that
+// changes to the upstream include list below never touch this hunk.
+#include "plainbrowser/win/msix_default_browser.h"
 
 #include <objbase.h>
 
@@ -789,6 +793,11 @@
 }
 
 DefaultWebClientState GetDefaultBrowser() {
+  // Plain Browser: from the MSIX package, ask by the package app's ID.
+  if (std::optional<bool> is_default =
+          plainbrowser::win::IsPackageDefaultBrowser()) {
+    return *is_default ? IS_DEFAULT : NOT_DEFAULT;
+  }
   return GetDefaultWebClientStateFromShellUtilDefaultState(
       ShellUtil::GetChromeDefaultState());
 }
@@ -868,6 +877,10 @@
   static constexpr std::wstring_view kSchemes[] = {L"http", L"https"};
   OpenSystemSettingsHelper::Begin(kSchemes, std::move(on_finished_callback));
 
+  // Plain Browser: from the MSIX package, open the package app's page.
+  if (plainbrowser::win::ShowPackageDefaultAppsSettings()) {
+    return;
+  }
   ShellUtil::ShowMakeChromeDefaultSystemUI(chrome_exe);
 }
 
